## Solved Question: Active Learning 1 (Demand curve shifts)
> **Question:** Draw a demand curve for music downloads. What happens to it in each of the following scenarios? Why?
> A. The price of iPods falls
> B. The price of music downloads falls
> C. The price of music CDs falls

**Step-by-Step Solution:**
- **A. The price of iPods falls:** iPods and music downloads are complements. A fall in the price of iPods increases the demand for music downloads. The Demand curve shifts **RIGHT**.
- **B. The price of music downloads falls:** This is a change in the price of the good itself! This does NOT shift the demand curve. Instead, it causes a **movement along** the demand curve to a point with a lower price and a higher quantity demanded.
- **C. The price of music CDs falls:** CDs and music downloads are substitutes. A fall in the price of CDs means people will buy more CDs and fewer downloads. The Demand curve shifts **LEFT**.

