## Solved Question: Active Learning 2 (Supply curve shifts)
> **Question:** Draw a supply curve for tax return preparation software. What happens to it in each of the following scenarios?
> A. Retailers cut the price of the software.
> B. A technological advance allows the software to be produced at lower cost.
> C. Professional tax return preparers raise the price of the services they provide.

**Step-by-Step Solution:**
- **A. Retailers cut the price of the software:** This is a change in the price of the good itself. This does NOT shift the supply curve. It causes a **movement along** the supply curve to a point with a lower price and lower quantity supplied.
- **B. A technological advance:** This reduces the cost of production. The Supply curve shifts **RIGHT**.
- **C. Professional tax return preparers raise the price of the services they provide:** This is a trick question! Professional preparers are a *substitute* for tax software. If they raise their prices, people will want to buy more software instead. This shifts the **Demand** curve for tax software to the right, not the Supply curve. The Supply curve does not shift.

